<title>HUNGARY: Hungary twelve-month bill yield rises to 20.45 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary twelve-month bill yield rises to 20.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of twelve-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 20.45 percent, up from 20.14 percent at an auction two weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	22,271.51 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 16,500 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield     20.45 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		83.1380 pct</p>
</text>
